<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.11.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02269</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.11.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>740fe479-dfd8-4875-a71f-5203520810af</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>For questions 1 – 4, identify a quadratic function in standard form, \(f(x)\), with the given zeros.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>1 and 9</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\(f(x) = x^2 + 10x + 9\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 8x + 9\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 8x + 9\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 10x + 9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2 − 10x + 9\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(\sqrt5\) and \(-\sqrt{5}\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 5x − 5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 5x − 5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 5\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2 − 5\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>–7</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 14x + 49\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 14x − 49\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 49\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 14x + 49\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2 + 14x + 49\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>–3</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 6x + 9\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 9\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 6x + 9\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2 + 6x + 9\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Examine the graph below to identify the zeros of the function. Then, write a quadratic function in standard form with the given zeros.</item>
</list>
<para>    <figure><media alt="A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 5 AND 1."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/d45d9f081db1b61ee2529b53e5c2892539aa57d7"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 4x − 5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 6x − 5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 4x − 5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 6x − 5\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2 + 4x − 5\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Examine the graph below to identify the zeros of the function. Then, write a quadratic function in standard form with the given zeros.</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH \(x\)-intercepts OF 2 AND 4."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3052dbda096476721907aeb22e7f73e814e56db2"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 2x − 8\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 6x + 8\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 2x − 8\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 6x + 8\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2 − 6x + 8\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write the specific quadratic function, \(p(x)\), in standard form, that has the zeros –8 and 3 and passes through the point \((2, -20)\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(p(x) = 2x^2 + 10x − 48\) </item>
  <item> \(p(x) = 3x^2 + 15x − 72\) </item>
  <item>\(p(x) = −x^2 − 5x − 6\) </item>
  <item> \(p(x) = x^2 + 5x − 24\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(p(x) = 2x^2 + 10x − 48\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write the specific quadratic function, \(g(x)\), in standard form, that has the zero 2 and passes through the point \((3, -3)\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(g(x) = x^2 − 4x + 4\) </item>
  <item> \(g(x) = 2x^2 − 8x + 3\) </item>
  <item> \(g(x) = −2x^2 + 8x − 8\) </item>
  <item> \(g(x) = −3x^2 + 12x − 12\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(g(x) = −3x^2 + 12x − 12\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write the specific quadratic function, \(h(x)\), in standard form, that has the zeros 3 and 5 and passes through the point \((2, 12)\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(h(x) = x^2 − 8x + 15\) </item>
  <item> \(h(x) = 4x^2 − 32x + 60\) </item>
  <item> \(h(x) = −x^2 + 8x − 15\) </item>
  <item> \(h(x) = 3x^2 − 24x + 48\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(h(x) = 4x^2 − 32x + 60\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write the specific quadratic function, \(w(x)\), in standard form, that has the zeros 6 and –7 and passes through the point \((5, 12)\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(w(x) = x^2 + x − 42\) </item>
  <item> \(w(x) = 2x^2 + 2x − 48\) </item>
  <item> \(w(x) = −2x^2 − 2x + 84\) </item>
  <item>\( w(x) = −x^2 − x + 42\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(w(x) = −x^2 − x + 42\)</para></section>
</content>
